### ─── IN-MEMORY MODE TEST SUITE ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### Start MoltenDB with the --in-memory flag (or MOLTENDB_IN_MEMORY=true) before
### running these requests. Data is stored only in RAM — nothing is written to the
### WAL log on disk. Restarting the server will wipe all data.
###
###   moltendb-server --in-memory --root-user admin --root-password admin123
###
### Collections used: `books` and `authors` — completely distinct from the
### laptops/memory/display collections used in other test files.
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### ─── STEP 1: Login ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

POST http://localhost:1538/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### Paste the token from the response here:
@token = eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJhZG1pbiIsImV4cCI6MTc4NDg2ODA5Miwic2NvcGVzIjpbIio6KjoqIl0sImp0aSI6ImZlMDNkNTViLWFhZmYtNDNmZS1hNDkxLTQ2ZWY1OTFhODQyMCJ9.0My50XFGTn2JP8ZaJ98IB_y-fPOrt5Im6HcKBfmLob8

### ─── STEP 2: Seed Data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### §1 and §2 must be run in order. Books reference authors via `author_id`.
### After seeding, restart the server and confirm all data is gone — that proves
### the in-memory mode is working and nothing was persisted to disk.

### §1. Seed the `authors` collection
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "authors",
  "data": {
    "auth1": {
      "name": "Frank Herbert",
      "nationality": "American",
      "born": 1920,
      "active": false
    },
    "auth2": {
      "name": "Ursula K. Le Guin",
      "nationality": "American",
      "born": 1929,
      "active": false
    },
    "auth3": {
      "name": "Liu Cixin",
      "nationality": "Chinese",
      "born": 1963,
      "active": true
    },
    "auth4": {
      "name": "N.K. Jemisin",
      "nationality": "American",
      "born": 1972,
      "active": true
    },
    "auth5": {
      "name": "Isaac Asimov",
      "nationality": "American",
      "born": 1920,
      "active": false
    }
  }
}

### §2. Seed the `books` collection
### Each book has a foreign key `author_id` pointing to the `authors` collection.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books",
  "data": {
    "bk1": {
      "title": "Dune",
      "author_id": "auth1",
      "year": 1965,
      "genre": "sci-fi",
      "pages": 412,
      "in_print": true,
      "rating": 4.8
    },
    "bk2": {
      "title": "The Left Hand of Darkness",
      "author_id": "auth2",
      "year": 1969,
      "genre": "sci-fi",
      "pages": 286,
      "in_print": true,
      "rating": 4.5
    },
    "bk3": {
      "title": "The Three-Body Problem",
      "author_id": "auth3",
      "year": 2008,
      "genre": "sci-fi",
      "pages": 400,
      "in_print": true,
      "rating": 4.6
    },
    "bk4": {
      "title": "The Fifth Season",
      "author_id": "auth4",
      "year": 2015,
      "genre": "fantasy",
      "pages": 468,
      "in_print": true,
      "rating": 4.7
    },
    "bk5": {
      "title": "Foundation",
      "author_id": "auth5",
      "year": 1951,
      "genre": "sci-fi",
      "pages": 244,
      "in_print": true,
      "rating": 4.6
    },
    "bk6": {
      "title": "Children of Dune",
      "author_id": "auth1",
      "year": 1976,
      "genre": "sci-fi",
      "pages": 444,
      "in_print": false,
      "rating": 4.2
    }
  }
}


### ─── STEP 3: Reads ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §3. Get all books — confirm all 6 are in RAM
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books",
  "fields": [
    "title",
    "year",
    "genre",
    "rating"
  ]
}

### §4. Filter — only sci-fi books with rating above 4.5
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books",
  "fields": [
    "title",
    "genre",
    "rating"
  ],
  "where": {
    "genre": "sci-fi",
    "rating": {
      "$gt": 4.5
    }
  },
  "sort": [
    {
      "field": "rating",
      "order": "desc"
    }
  ]
}

### §5. Join — books with their author details embedded
### Expected: each book document gets an `author` object with name + nationality
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books",
  "fields": [
    "title",
    "year",
    "rating"
  ],
  "joins": [
    {
      "author": {
        "from": "authors",
        "on": "author_id",
        "fields": [
          "name",
          "nationality"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "sort": [
    {
      "field": "year",
      "order": "asc"
    }
  ]
}

### §6. Join with WHERE — only currently in-print books, with full author info
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books",
  "fields": [
    "title",
    "genre",
    "in_print"
  ],
  "joins": [
    {
      "author": {
        "from": "authors",
        "on": "author_id"
      }
    }
  ],
  "where": {
    "in_print": true
  }
}


### ─── STEP 4: Updates ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §7. Update a single book — mark "Children of Dune" back in print and fix rating
### Confirm the change is visible immediately (RAM update, no WAL flush needed)
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books",
  "data": {
    "bk6": {
      "title": "Children of Dune",
      "author_id": "auth1",
      "year": 1976,
      "genre": "sci-fi",
      "pages": 444,
      "in_print": true,
      "rating": 4.4
    }
  }
}

### §8. Verify the update — bk6 should now show in_print: true and rating: 4.4
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books",
  "where": {
    "title": {
      "$contains": "Children"
    }
  }
}

### §9. Update an author — Liu Cixin wins an award, bump his record
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "authors",
  "data": {
    "auth3": {
      "name": "Liu Cixin",
      "nationality": "Chinese",
      "born": 1963,
      "active": true,
      "awards": [
        "Hugo Award"
      ]
    }
  }
}


### ─── STEP 5: Deletes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §10. Delete a book — remove "Foundation" from the in-memory store
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books",
  "keys": [
    "bk5"
  ]
}

### §11. Confirm deletion — get all books, bk5 (Foundation) should be gone
### Expected: 5 books returned, no Foundation entry
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books",
  "fields": [
    "title",
    "author_id"
  ],
  "sort": [
    {
      "field": "title",
      "order": "asc"
    }
  ]
}

### §12. Delete an author — remove Isaac Asimov (whose book was already deleted)
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "authors",
  "keys": [
    "auth5"
  ]
}


### ─── STEP 6: Persistence Check (manual) ────────────────────────────────────
### Stop the server (Ctrl+C) and restart it with --in-memory again.
### Then run §3 again — the response should be empty (no books), proving that
### nothing was written to disk and the RAM store was wiped on shutdown.
###
###   Expected after restart: { "data": [], "count": 0 }

### §13. Post-restart check — should return empty (no data survived the restart)
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "books"
}
